# Debug: the double free is fatal (exit code 3) and the fatal report lists the live objects (the
# deliberate leak of node b1). Release has no checks: the second Delete runs the destructor again
# through the freed object, then the C heap or the processor catches it (Windows: the heap's double
# free report; Linux: the freed vtable faults), which the runtime turns into a fatal error, exit code 3;
# only the output before the second Delete is compared.
== exit Debug
3
== exit Release
3
